  "comment": "Tag membership (SCHEMA.md 'Tags'): any page can be assigned as a tag to pages AND blocks. Two parentless tag pages (Tag A, Tag B) are created first; the content node is created with tagIds [A] (the OR-Set seed). A re-issued object.create {objectId, tagIds:[B]} on the EXISTING node is the assign carrier — the applier's alreadyExists branch upserts tag_member_set without touching the tree, so tag_ids reads [A, B] (recomputeTagIds sorts by tag_id). tag.unassign {objectId, tagId: A} tombstones the pair: tag_ids reads [B] only. The final re-issued object.create {objectId, tagIds:[A]} with a NEWER hlc than the tombstone resurrects A — the deliberate add-wins asymmetry (the tag add's actor tiebreak is strictly-greater '>', vs the classIds '>=').",
